        {
            "Section": "IT.SUCAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "SUCAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What is/was the category of the substance (used)?\nSubstance Used Category [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 1,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": 12,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "SUCAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "SUCAT [CDASH]\nRecord the Substance Used category, if not preprinted on the CRF. [completionInstructions]\nSponsor-defined controlled terminology (e.g., TOBACCO, ALCOHOL, CAFFEINE). Sponsors may require different types of substance use data (e.g., illicit drug use, cigarettes); the value for category may be preprinted on the CRF. If a more detailed type of substance appears on the CRF (e.g., CIGARETTES, CIGARS, rather than TOBACCO), SUCAT is TOBACCO and SUTRT is CIGARETTES. If the sponsor does not specify a type of tobacco on the CRF, SUTRT is TOBACCO. If SUCAT is not collected (e.g. it is self-evident from the protocol design), it could be populated during the SDTM-based dataset creation process. [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. [mappingInstructions]\n[Substance (Used) Category]; NULL [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.SUNCF",
            "Unnamed: 1": "SUNCF",
            "Unnamed: 2": "Has the subject ever used tobacco? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 2,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": "CL.C78738.NCF",
            "Unnamed: 7": 7,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "SUNCF\nHas the subject ever [used/consumed] [SUTRT/SUCAT]? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "SUNCF [CDASH]\nCheck the appropriate box to indicate if the subject has ever used/consumed tobacco/alcohol/caffeine, currently consumes tobacco/alcohol/caffeine, or formerly used/consumed tobacco/alcohol/caffeine. [completionInstructions]\nThe 3 options (NEVER, CURRENT, FORMER) are sponsor-defined in relation to the protocol. If the sponsor has specific definitions, these definitions are detailed in the instructions to the site. As this type of response does not correspond exactly to an SDTM variable, CDASH recommends using the CDASHIG variable SUNCF. Sponsors must decide how to populate the appropriate relative timing variables when the SDTM-based datasets are created. For example, If SUNCF =\"Never\", the value of SUOCCUR will be \"N\" and all relative timing variables will be null. If the sponsor chooses to populate the relative start references (SUSTRTPT, SUSTRF) the value will be \"BEFORE\" when SUNCF= \"CURRENT\" and \"FORMER\". If the sponsor also chooses to use relative end references (SUENRF, SUENRTPT) , the SUENRTPT value will be \"ONGOING\" when SUNCF=\"CURREN\" while the value of SUENRF will be \"DURING/AFTER\".   Note: When using SUSTRTPT and/or SUENRTPT, these must refer to a \"time point anchor\" such as SCREENING in SUSTTPT/SUENTPT. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. May be used to populate SUOCCUR and relative timing variables. [mappingInstructions]\n([Substance]) Usage [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
