            "Unnamed: 11": "SUTRT [CDASH]\nSponsors may require different types of substance use data (e.g., illicit drug use, cigarettes); the value for category may be preprinted on the CRF as a label for the prompt for Substance Use. If a more detailed type of substance appears on the CRF (e.g., CIGARETTES, CIGARS rather than TOBACCO), SUCAT should be TOBACCO and SUTRT should be CIGARETTES. [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. [mappingInstructions]\n[Type of Substance] [prompt]",
